WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.169
Today is the most significant day in the

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.671
history of the NCAA.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:08.925
The last day on planet earth,

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:10.760
in the United States of America

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.554
in college athletics, where name, image,

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:15.473
and likeness laws will
not be on the books.

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:18.810
And kids will be not allowed
to make money off of their

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.520
name, image and likeness.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.483
Today's the last day that
amateurism has at least a shadow

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.444
meaning in our culture.

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:29.654
Major ruling from the Supreme
court involving the end.

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:32.532
The most seismic change in
college sports happened in 2021

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.410
and it's aftershocks are
still ricocheting across the

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.619
landscape.

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:39.622
Non-pro athletes getting
paid for use of their name,

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:43.209
image and likeness until last
year banned by the NCAA is now

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:47.088
allowed and it's changing the
face of sports and business

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.673
radically.

00:00:48.673 --> 00:00:51.551
According to opendorse,
brands spent almost a billion

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:54.429
dollars in the first year of
the new rules and that number

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:58.058
is only going to grow, but
some of the biggest winners,

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.809
they may surprise you.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:03.104
Top female athletes are cashing
in and women's basketball

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:05.940
players are standing center stage.

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:09.235
Your heels. You want
your heels to go down,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.737
His poop stinks.

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:14.532
He took a pre-ride poop.

00:01:14.532 --> 00:01:16.659
NIL it really is pretty surreal.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.120
I don't think I really wrapped
my head around the concept

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.538
that I am making money,

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:21.539
just doing the thing that I love.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.545
Starting her sophomore year,

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:28.671
Azzi Fudd's already signed deals

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:29.547
with Chipotle,

00:01:29.547 --> 00:01:30.507
American Eagle,

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:31.341
and others.

00:01:31.341 --> 00:01:33.093
Earning tens of thousands of dollars,

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:36.096
leveraging her on-court
prowess and off-court

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.972
social media following.

00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:39.974
She's also getting massive investment

00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:41.226
from the pro game as well,

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:44.104
becoming one of the first
athletes to sign with Steph

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.063
Curry's,

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:46.356
SC30 Inc.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.025
The two even designed a shoe together.

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:52.654
One Steph Curry would wear
during his 2021 NBA finals,

00:01:52.654 --> 00:01:54.489
MVP performance.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.535
It's an investment directly
into a future player,

00:01:58.535 --> 00:02:00.829
but also the future of women's basketball.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:02.956
And especially for the women's game,

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.625
NIL deals may not only
benefit the students,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.377
but the pro game as well.

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:15.635
Wait, I'm gonna call.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.554
Carly knows everything.

00:02:19.889 --> 00:02:20.723
Hey.

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:21.558
Hi, Carly.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:23.935
I have my TV mounted
on the wall of my room,

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:27.897
and I'm wondering if I'm
moving back into the same room.

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:30.400
Can I just take the TV
off and leave them mount?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.234
Kind of all

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:34.737
the little things that I
said I have too much of.

00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:36.114
Azzi Fudd can almost trick you

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:38.449
into thinking she's just
a regular college student.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:41.077
You can't judge me by
what you see here today.

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:45.331
We just finished our summer session.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.416
So I'm about to move out.

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:47.625
I gotta completely move out

00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:48.459
to re-move in to the exact same

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:49.294
apartment.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.046
Starting to stress me out.

00:02:52.046 --> 00:02:54.048
I gotta carry this back.

00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:57.677
Who's gonna help you move

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.053
all the big stuff though?

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:00.054
Oh, well you see, I leave tomorrow.

00:03:00.054 --> 00:03:04.601
So I will be probably
pulling an all nighter.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.311
But not if my mom is watching this,

00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:07.937
I will be going to sleep early.

00:03:07.937 --> 00:03:09.564
And getting my rest.

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:12.734
Don't let a messy dorm room

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.152
and procrastination fool you, though.

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.153
It's very clear,

00:03:15.153 --> 00:03:18.948
very quick that there is
nothing ordinary about her.

00:03:20.074 --> 00:03:22.827
Fudd was the class of 2021's number one,

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:25.288
consensus recruit while she
was playing for St.John's

00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:26.122
college,

00:03:26.122 --> 00:03:27.790
high school out of DC.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.043
Now she's playing for one of
the most storied and winning

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.212
programs in any sport in history,

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.339
the University of Connecticut Huskies.

00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:35.715
The National championship

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.759
goes to Connecticut for the fourth

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:39.594
year in a row.

00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:40.678
As the dynasty

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:42.430
fulfills its destiny.

00:03:43.473 --> 00:03:45.225
Winners of 11 national championships,

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.726
producers of Olympians,

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:50.396
and multiple WNBA MVPs,

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.607
but Azzi has something
that the trailblazing women

00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:54.359
of UConn's past never had:

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:57.445
the opportunity to not
only play basketball,

00:03:57.445 --> 00:03:59.113
but get paid for it.

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:02.450
I remember just learning that
you could profit off of your

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.120
name and brand,

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.331
and I could profit off of Azzi,

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:09.123
the basketball player,

00:04:09.123 --> 00:04:10.333
not just Azzi the person,

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:12.752
which I didn't really
understand why you couldn't,

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.380
because at least for me like
Azzi the basketball player

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.882
is also Azzi the person.

00:04:17.882 --> 00:04:20.593
Like basketball is such
a huge role in my life

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.221
that I didn't understand why
I wouldn't be able to profit

00:04:23.221 --> 00:04:24.055
from it.

00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:27.267
It's important to
understand exactly what made

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.226
this all possible.

00:04:28.226 --> 00:04:29.435
In 2021,

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.979
after decades of debate,

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:32.563
lawsuits and legislation,

00:04:32.563 --> 00:04:35.316
the NCAA prompted by a unanimous ruling

00:04:35.316 --> 00:04:36.526
by the Supreme Court,

00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:40.113
finally relented on one of its
longest standing strictures,

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:43.491
that athletes could not in
any way be compensated beyond

00:04:43.491 --> 00:04:46.661
scholarships and small
stipends from their schools.

00:04:46.661 --> 00:04:48.413
It would only take a
few months before Azzi,

00:04:48.413 --> 00:04:50.415
a freshman at the time,

00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:53.209
would sign her first
major deal with Chipotle.

00:04:53.209 --> 00:04:55.378
Before the freshman even got to play

00:04:55.378 --> 00:04:56.379
a game for the Huskies,

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:59.924
she inks her first NIL deal as
a college athlete ambassador

00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:03.261
for the magnificent
Mexican restaurant chain.

00:05:03.261 --> 00:05:08.266
You are on the leading edge
of something that feels,

00:05:09.017 --> 00:05:11.394
for those of us who've
been looking at sports

00:05:11.394 --> 00:05:12.228
for a long time,

00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:14.397
a very meaningful moment in sports.

00:05:14.397 --> 00:05:16.024
The economics are changing.

00:05:16.024 --> 00:05:20.278
The role of sports and
society is changing.

00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:21.362
We see that from the outside,

00:05:21.362 --> 00:05:22.238
you're inside it.

00:05:22.238 --> 00:05:25.241
Does it feel momentous to you?

00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:27.910
You can tell how important it is,

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:28.995
but at the same time,

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.664
this is all I know in
college basketball's NIL,

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:34.584
so I'm still trying to find my way in it,

00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:36.169
find my groove and stuff,

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:40.757
but I know how important it
is and kind of like the people

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:43.760
before me paved the way and
set that path for me to be able

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.596
to do this and how important
it is for me to be able to take

00:05:46.596 --> 00:05:49.015
advantage of this and be able
to continue this on for the

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:50.933
athletes to come.

00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:53.102
While colleges and universities

00:05:53.102 --> 00:05:55.271
still can't directly
compensate their athletes,

00:05:55.271 --> 00:05:58.066
those athletes can legally be
paid by third parties who want

00:05:58.066 --> 00:05:58.983
to use their name,

00:05:58.983 --> 00:05:59.942
image and likeness,

00:05:59.942 --> 00:06:00.777
or NIL.

00:06:02.111 --> 00:06:02.945
Azzi,

00:06:02.945 --> 00:06:05.698
advised closely by a team led
by her parents and her agents,

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.700
has created a portfolio anchored by

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.535
relationships with Chipotle,

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.370
American Eagle,

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.996
sports drink BioSteel,

00:06:11.996 --> 00:06:13.039
and SC30.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:16.292
Brands she already admired
as a successful athlete and

00:06:16.292 --> 00:06:18.419
American teenager.

00:06:18.419 --> 00:06:20.380
I've been lucky that the deals that

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.506
the deals I've been approached
with have been things

00:06:21.506 --> 00:06:23.466
that have been really good and things

00:06:23.466 --> 00:06:24.384
that I had liked.

00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:26.594
Like American Eagle is
one of my favorite brands.

00:06:26.594 --> 00:06:27.428
I always wear their jeans.

00:06:27.428 --> 00:06:31.641
So it was like one of the
easiest transitions type things.

00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:34.811
BioSteel was something that
I hadn't really tried before.

00:06:34.811 --> 00:06:36.062
And once I did,

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.230
I really liked it.

00:06:42.985 --> 00:06:44.320
On the basketball side,

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:46.197
it's impossible to be on UConn's campus

00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:47.990
and not feel the weight of history.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.536
Especially when you see
where the team works out.

00:06:51.536 --> 00:06:52.495
Officially called the

00:06:52.495 --> 00:06:55.623
Werth Family UConn
Basketball Champion Center,

00:06:55.623 --> 00:06:58.918
it's a 78,200 square foot complex,

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.671
that costs 40 million dollars.

00:07:01.671 --> 00:07:02.922
It's most striking feature?

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:04.966
It's split right down the middle

00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:07.510
between men's and women's basketball.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.554
Seemingly identical when you walk in,

00:07:09.554 --> 00:07:10.388
except,

00:07:10.388 --> 00:07:12.098
while the men's team boasts
four national championships,

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:15.143
the women's side has
more than double that.

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:17.770
And that actually
understates their dominance.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.189
The team has gone
undefeated in six seasons

00:07:20.189 --> 00:07:23.317
and its players have been
staples on the US Olympic team,

00:07:23.317 --> 00:07:26.863
Sue Bird and Diana Taurasi are
only the latest in the line

00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:27.697
of superstars,

00:07:27.697 --> 00:07:29.782
that began in the early 1990s with

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:30.992
Rebecca Lobo.

00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:34.162
The Huskies have featured
12 AP national players

00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:35.121
of the year,

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.164
including Lobo,

00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:37.206
Maya Moore - twice,

00:07:37.206 --> 00:07:39.417
Breanna Stewart - three times.

00:07:39.417 --> 00:07:40.543
And most recently,

00:07:40.543 --> 00:07:41.794
Paige Bueckers.

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.212
We'll get to her in a minute.

00:07:44.547 --> 00:07:46.090
Banners are,

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:46.924
I mean,

00:07:46.924 --> 00:07:48.176
they're overwhelming for me

00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:50.803
and I'm not sitting and standing

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:51.846
in your shoes.

00:07:51.846 --> 00:07:53.973
What do you take from that personally?

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:56.684
I think it can be seen
for sure as overwhelming,

00:07:56.684 --> 00:07:59.437
kind of pressure to live
up to those standards.

00:07:59.437 --> 00:08:02.940
But I use it kind of as motivation.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:04.233
This is our UConn program.

00:08:04.233 --> 00:08:06.277
Like, there's no need to
compare ourselves to the past.

00:08:06.277 --> 00:08:08.112
We're not those players
that we see on the wall.

00:08:08.112 --> 00:08:09.113
We're different players.

00:08:09.113 --> 00:08:09.947
Like I'm Azzi.

00:08:09.947 --> 00:08:10.781
I'm not Sue Bird

00:08:10.781 --> 00:08:13.451
We need to forge our own
path and our own story

00:08:13.451 --> 00:08:14.952
in the UConn books

00:08:16.913 --> 00:08:18.164
These former UConn stars
help to establish the

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.833
UConn team as a product to watch.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.168
Over the last decade,

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:24.587
Media rights moved from
Connecticut Public Television

00:08:24.587 --> 00:08:27.798
to SNY and now include Fox Sports.

00:08:27.798 --> 00:08:29.008
With game coverage mixed with

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:30.551
behind-the-scenes documentaries,

00:08:30.551 --> 00:08:33.387
UConn has become one of the
biggest platforms for women's

00:08:33.387 --> 00:08:35.097
basketball.

00:08:35.097 --> 00:08:37.266
The UConn women's team is so well known,

00:08:37.266 --> 00:08:38.476
that at the moment,

00:08:38.476 --> 00:08:39.310
it's arguably a better platform than most,

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:43.606
if not all of the professional
women's teams or even the

00:08:43.606 --> 00:08:45.066
WNBA overall.

00:08:45.942 --> 00:08:46.776
Well,

00:08:46.776 --> 00:08:49.111
I don't think there's any
greater female sports collegiate

00:08:49.111 --> 00:08:52.156
brand than the UConn Women's Basketball.

00:08:52.156 --> 00:08:53.032
It's on TV.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:56.369
You can follow those athletes
in a way that if you compare

00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:57.203
it to the WNBA,

00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:59.830
you don't always get
consistency of coverage,

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:02.667
local or international markets.

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:05.169
You're not always able
to follow those athletes.

00:09:05.169 --> 00:09:06.837
Feels so nice to be back.

00:09:06.837 --> 00:09:08.130
This is Angela Ruggiero.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.550
She's a former hockey player
and four-time Olympian.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.344
She now runs Sports Innovation Lab.

00:09:13.344 --> 00:09:15.763
That's a Boston based company
that uses data science to help

00:09:15.763 --> 00:09:20.309
teams and leagues understand
their fans and figure out how

00:09:20.309 --> 00:09:22.270
to better engage them.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.980
The future of sports really is

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.232
how do you optimize and drive

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:28.234
revenue in these digital spaces,

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:29.610
these digital communities.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.112
So collegiate athletes,

00:09:31.112 --> 00:09:32.071
I think,

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.240
are gonna really benefit
from the change in the NIL

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.910
ecosystem because they're
authentically themselves.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.496
They're using these platforms
already and they're being

00:09:40.496 --> 00:09:41.581
entertainers.

00:09:42.498 --> 00:09:44.333
Not sure how to work this.

00:09:44.333 --> 00:09:45.710
I think it's recording.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:48.462
Fans of women's sports and
female athletes want more

00:09:48.462 --> 00:09:49.880
authenticity.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:53.134
These fans are dying for not
just the game and the stats and

00:09:53.134 --> 00:09:54.760
the scores. They wanna
know what you're doing.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.095
24/7.

00:09:56.095 --> 00:09:58.389
They wanna know what these
female athletes think,

00:09:58.389 --> 00:09:59.307
what are they wearing?

00:09:59.307 --> 00:10:00.725
Who are they dating?

00:10:00.725 --> 00:10:01.559
What do they care about?

00:10:01.559 --> 00:10:02.768
What are their causes?

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:06.772
And that's gonna build a wave
of support when those athletes

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:10.568
graduate that they'll
hopefully bring to those WNBA

00:10:10.568 --> 00:10:12.111
teams.

00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:13.613
I think that this is really an

00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:14.739
incredible opportunity for me

00:10:14.739 --> 00:10:17.700
and all of women's basketball
to be able to benefit

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.161
and it's sad knowing that
this is kind of our most

00:10:20.161 --> 00:10:21.412
profitable age.

00:10:22.496 --> 00:10:25.082
So I think that that's also a big,

00:10:25.082 --> 00:10:26.917
an important part of

00:10:26.917 --> 00:10:30.212
being able to use NIL
now before going pro.

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:42.516
But dance videos and homemade
Tostino's ads can only take

00:10:42.516 --> 00:10:44.977
that mission so far.

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:47.688
Azzi knows that success
on the court comes first,

00:10:47.688 --> 00:10:50.858
and allow everything else to follow.

00:10:50.858 --> 00:10:52.818
And while UConn has had a storied history,

00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:57.156
their last championship
was way back in 2016.

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:59.909
Lucky for her she's playing
with not only just a good friend

00:10:59.909 --> 00:11:00.910
and dance partner,

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.454
but the best college
player in the country.

00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:04.955
Paige Bueckers

00:11:04.955 --> 00:11:07.124
Paige "Buckets" Bueckers

00:11:07.124 --> 00:11:09.335
is also one of the biggest
college students when it

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:10.628
comes to NIL deals.

00:11:10.628 --> 00:11:12.797
Striking the first NCAA athlete deal

00:11:12.797 --> 00:11:13.839
with Gatorade,

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:18.010
as well as partnerships
with StockX and Cash App.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.513
And she has been estimated to
potentially bring in a million

00:11:20.513 --> 00:11:22.264
dollars in NIL deals.

00:11:24.266 --> 00:11:25.476
We do a lot of team

00:11:25.476 --> 00:11:27.937
This is your first time horse riding.

00:11:27.937 --> 00:11:29.438
Yes.

00:11:29.438 --> 00:11:32.525
This is my first one
involving a live animal.

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:35.069
During the last week of
official summer workouts,

00:11:35.069 --> 00:11:35.903
Azzi, Paige,

00:11:35.903 --> 00:11:37.988
and their teammates finished
their last session and

00:11:37.988 --> 00:11:39.865
went over to UConn's horse barn

00:11:39.865 --> 00:11:41.701
for some team bonding.

00:11:45.371 --> 00:11:46.205
I have an extra large.

00:11:46.205 --> 00:11:49.166
Right? So when you're
working with the horses,

00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:51.544
you wanna try to stay calm and relaxed.

00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:53.129
You're gonna make him anxious.

00:11:53.129 --> 00:11:53.963
I'm sorry.

00:11:53.963 --> 00:11:55.798
It's typical day in Storrs, Connecticut.

00:11:55.798 --> 00:11:59.885
That's what we do when we
don't play basketball,.

00:12:00.928 --> 00:12:02.388
Peasants,

00:12:02.388 --> 00:12:03.222
farewell.

00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:06.100
It was a light moment
before everyone went off

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:07.643
to hang with their families and

00:12:07.643 --> 00:12:10.271
get rested up for the season.

00:12:10.271 --> 00:12:11.480
A few weeks later,

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:14.567
Bueckers would announce
that her 22-23 season

00:12:14.567 --> 00:12:17.194
was over before it even started.

00:12:17.194 --> 00:12:18.487
UConn women's basketball,

00:12:18.487 --> 00:12:19.363
junior guard,

00:12:19.363 --> 00:12:20.364
Paige Beckers,

00:12:20.364 --> 00:12:23.534
suffered a torn ACL in
her left knee and will

00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:26.704
miss the 2022-23 season.

00:12:26.704 --> 00:12:29.248
It's an injury Azzi knows all too well.

00:12:29.248 --> 00:12:33.502
Having gone through her
own ACL tear in 2019.

00:12:33.502 --> 00:12:36.672
While Paige's absence will test
the team's depth and mettle.

00:12:36.672 --> 00:12:38.716
What was on display in Storrs

00:12:38.716 --> 00:12:40.634
and apparent in conversations with Azzi

00:12:40.634 --> 00:12:43.179
was that she and Bueckers
were intent on using their

00:12:43.179 --> 00:12:44.847
increasingly higher profiles,

00:12:44.847 --> 00:12:48.934
not just to benefit themselves,
but their entire team.

00:12:48.934 --> 00:12:49.935
Bruh,

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:50.770
Paige.

00:12:51.687 --> 00:12:52.897
No, you didn't.

00:12:54.106 --> 00:12:56.484
Aww, she's so sweet.

00:12:57.526 --> 00:12:59.570
Oh, I'm so excited.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.571
In Azzi's case,

00:13:00.571 --> 00:13:03.073
that means free Chipotle.

00:13:03.073 --> 00:13:04.658
Thanks.

00:13:04.658 --> 00:13:06.118
Both Azzi and Paige are conscious

00:13:06.118 --> 00:13:09.205
of the inequality that
still exists in NIL,

00:13:09.205 --> 00:13:11.040
while all the players
in this room share the

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.875
benefit of playing at UConn,

00:13:12.875 --> 00:13:14.376
not all can or will get the deals

00:13:14.376 --> 00:13:16.712
Azzi and Paige have already signed.

00:13:16.712 --> 00:13:18.672
Sophomores. You first, since I catered.

00:13:18.672 --> 00:13:22.051
People outside of your
world of actually doing it,

00:13:22.051 --> 00:13:26.055
speculate about the consequences
and maybe some of the

00:13:26.055 --> 00:13:28.641
unintended consequences of NIL you think,

00:13:28.641 --> 00:13:29.475
well,

00:13:29.475 --> 00:13:31.101
the really prominent players,

00:13:31.101 --> 00:13:34.730
like you are gonna benefit and
then other players are not.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:39.735
And so maybe there's some
jealousy or envy or whatever.

00:13:39.735 --> 00:13:41.654
How do you make sure that it doesn't?

00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:42.488
We are very tight.

00:13:42.488 --> 00:13:43.864
We're a super close group.

00:13:43.864 --> 00:13:44.698
I mean,

00:13:44.698 --> 00:13:45.533
you've been to Storrs,

00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:47.660
there's not much else to do
besides play basketball and

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.036
hang out with each other.

00:13:49.036 --> 00:13:52.164
And I think it also is because
that whatever deals we get,

00:13:52.164 --> 00:13:53.082
we share with each other.

00:13:53.082 --> 00:13:55.668
So I have a deal with
Chipotle and my whole team,

00:13:55.668 --> 00:13:56.544
whenever they want Chipotle,

00:13:56.544 --> 00:13:57.378
they let me know,

00:13:57.378 --> 00:13:58.212
or American Eagle,

00:13:58.212 --> 00:13:59.547
they can get whatever they want.

00:13:59.547 --> 00:14:00.381
They just let me know.

00:14:00.381 --> 00:14:02.049
And I think it goes both ways
with whatever deals other

00:14:02.049 --> 00:14:05.469
people have that we're super open and

00:14:05.469 --> 00:14:07.346
always willing to share.

00:14:07.346 --> 00:14:09.014
I think I'm posting on
Instagram about this.

00:14:09.014 --> 00:14:11.517
This would be the last team meal for Azzi

00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:12.935
before going on summer break,

00:14:12.935 --> 00:14:14.478
and when we next caught up with her,

00:14:14.478 --> 00:14:16.564
it would be about as far from
a dorm room in Storrs that you

00:14:16.564 --> 00:14:18.148
could possibly get.

00:14:21.485 --> 00:14:23.571
Azzi's out in LA this week
to do a commercial shoot

00:14:23.571 --> 00:14:25.155
for a new Under Armour shoe,

00:14:25.155 --> 00:14:27.575
alongside both Steph and Seth Curry,

00:14:27.575 --> 00:14:29.368
along with her is her family,

00:14:29.368 --> 00:14:32.580
including her former coaches
and current business screens,

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.123
her mom and dad.

00:14:34.123 --> 00:14:36.876
We make sure that that one
of us is at everything she

00:14:36.876 --> 00:14:38.961
does just to give her that support.

00:14:38.961 --> 00:14:41.046
So I've been at a lot of
them still blows my mind,

00:14:41.046 --> 00:14:41.881
like,

00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:42.715
okay,

00:14:42.715 --> 00:14:43.632
wow you look really cute in that outfit,

00:14:43.632 --> 00:14:45.092
but it just doesn't like really,

00:14:45.092 --> 00:14:46.218
I don't know,

00:14:46.218 --> 00:14:47.261
sink in that,

00:14:47.261 --> 00:14:51.640
that she's this public figure
for lack of a better word.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:55.603
The partnership with Curry is
both historic and important.

00:14:55.603 --> 00:14:57.021
Well beyond the deal itself.

00:14:57.021 --> 00:14:58.689
Azzi was the first woman and the

00:14:58.689 --> 00:15:00.399
first college athlete to join

00:15:00.399 --> 00:15:04.904
the SC30 brand and has developed
a friendship with Curry.

00:15:04.904 --> 00:15:06.989
She fully concedes to initially being

00:15:06.989 --> 00:15:08.240
a bit starstruck.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.658
Oh, it's kind of crazy.

00:15:09.658 --> 00:15:10.492
I mean,

00:15:10.492 --> 00:15:12.536
I try to keep my cool
when I'm working out with

00:15:12.536 --> 00:15:15.456
him and then with Seth and stuff on set,

00:15:15.456 --> 00:15:16.582
but in my head,

00:15:16.582 --> 00:15:17.833
I'm going a little bit crazy.

00:15:17.833 --> 00:15:19.293
Yeah.

00:15:19.293 --> 00:15:21.503
I first met him at Curry Camp,

00:15:21.503 --> 00:15:23.422
right after my freshman
year in high school.

00:15:23.422 --> 00:15:24.381
I got invited.

00:15:24.381 --> 00:15:26.926
I was one of the first
two girls invited to camp.

00:15:26.926 --> 00:15:29.470
And then I was invited
the next year as well.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:32.097
And then Curry brand
reached out to my agent

00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:34.433
at my group and they let me know,

00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:36.810
and I was all for it.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:39.313
I'm working out with
someone that I look up to

00:15:39.313 --> 00:15:41.065
and someone that inspires me.

00:15:41.065 --> 00:15:44.777
So getting to see firsthand
like him in action,

00:15:44.777 --> 00:15:47.613
what he does behind the scenes.

00:15:47.613 --> 00:15:51.992
I get to challenge myself and
compete a little bit with him.

00:15:51.992 --> 00:15:53.077
It's amazing.

00:15:55.579 --> 00:15:57.331
Shooting ads for unreleased apparel

00:15:57.331 --> 00:15:59.583
isn't something cameras were welcome into,

00:15:59.583 --> 00:16:01.377
but Azzi is also in LA for basketball,

00:16:01.377 --> 00:16:04.588
getting private workouts with
Steph Curry's own trainer,

00:16:04.588 --> 00:16:06.340
Carl Bergstrom.

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:08.425
Azzi's also been a part of Curry Camps,

00:16:08.425 --> 00:16:10.719
including this past
summer in San Francisco.

00:16:10.719 --> 00:16:13.514
She also helped design
a shoe for the SC30 line

00:16:13.514 --> 00:16:16.350
that Curry himself wore
in an NBA finals game

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:17.559
this past season.

00:16:17.559 --> 00:16:21.814
The 2022 Bill Russell NBA finals MVP award

00:16:21.814 --> 00:16:23.649
goes to Stephan Curry.

00:16:26.068 --> 00:16:27.611
Did you know that on average,

00:16:27.611 --> 00:16:29.863
women have 30% less income for retirement?

00:16:29.863 --> 00:16:32.408
TIAA was one of the first
brands where I got to use my

00:16:32.408 --> 00:16:37.079
platform taught to speak out
about Title IX and retirement

00:16:37.079 --> 00:16:38.122
equality.

00:16:38.122 --> 00:16:40.332
I think that's definitely
something that I still wanna

00:16:40.332 --> 00:16:41.166
continue to do,

00:16:41.166 --> 00:16:43.502
but that was big for me because
I'm still trying to figure

00:16:43.502 --> 00:16:48.007
out what I stand for and what
I support and things I wanna

00:16:48.007 --> 00:16:49.591
be able to support.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:54.471
She's gotta formulate
her own understanding

00:16:54.471 --> 00:16:56.682
and opinion about life.

00:16:56.682 --> 00:17:00.060
We all have our own perspectives
and that's what makes us

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:00.894
all unique.

00:17:00.894 --> 00:17:02.730
We all have our own
opinions and experiences

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.064
and I'm just proud

00:17:04.064 --> 00:17:06.650
that she found a level of
comfort to be able to speak on

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.944
something that she had no idea existed.

00:17:08.944 --> 00:17:10.654
I didn't know existed.

00:17:10.654 --> 00:17:11.613
Retirement inequality,

00:17:11.613 --> 00:17:15.659
women retire with 30% less
income in retirement than men.

00:17:15.659 --> 00:17:17.036
I didn't know that was a thing.

00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:19.413
And I think from being a girl-dad,

00:17:19.413 --> 00:17:23.250
having her come along has
awakened my senses to things that

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:25.252
my wife has experienced as a player,

00:17:25.252 --> 00:17:26.962
that I've seen firsthand,

00:17:26.962 --> 00:17:28.589
being a girls' basketball coach,

00:17:28.589 --> 00:17:31.383
that the girls endure.

00:17:31.383 --> 00:17:34.178
It's been pretty tremendous, honestly.

00:17:35.679 --> 00:17:36.889
And as a fellow girl-dad,

00:17:36.889 --> 00:17:39.224
Curry's involvement with
an equality campaign was

00:17:39.224 --> 00:17:40.059
notable,

00:17:40.059 --> 00:17:42.811
but not surprising for Azzi
who said she was drawn to his

00:17:42.811 --> 00:17:45.397
brand as much for his
off-the-court persona as his

00:17:45.397 --> 00:17:47.441
championship pedigree.

00:17:47.441 --> 00:17:50.069
He is a very big family man.

00:17:50.069 --> 00:17:51.236
You can see that with his kids,

00:17:51.236 --> 00:17:52.446
with his wife.

00:17:52.446 --> 00:17:53.906
And I'm huge with my family.

00:17:53.906 --> 00:17:55.324
I do everything with them.

00:17:55.324 --> 00:17:56.867
They're with me here on this trip.

00:17:56.867 --> 00:17:59.453
So I think the family aspect
was huge and just kind of his

00:17:59.453 --> 00:18:00.329
personality.

00:18:00.329 --> 00:18:01.872
He welcomed me in right away.

00:18:01.872 --> 00:18:02.998
Even when I was at camp,

00:18:02.998 --> 00:18:06.627
he made me feel part of
that group and special

00:18:06.627 --> 00:18:07.669
just being here.

00:18:07.669 --> 00:18:10.547
I feel like I'm really part
of this part of this brand,

00:18:10.547 --> 00:18:11.381
part of this team,

00:18:11.381 --> 00:18:12.841
part of the Curry family.

00:18:12.841 --> 00:18:14.760
And I couldn't be more grateful

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:15.594
Kobe Bryant,

00:18:15.594 --> 00:18:16.428
forever,

00:18:16.428 --> 00:18:17.262
of course remembered as an NBA legend and

00:18:17.262 --> 00:18:18.097
rightfully so,

00:18:18.097 --> 00:18:19.598
but as a father of four daughters -

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:22.142
Curry's also filled a void that Azzi

00:18:22.142 --> 00:18:23.227
and others thought might be

00:18:23.227 --> 00:18:25.813
left empty after Kobe Bryant
and his daughter Gigi,

00:18:25.813 --> 00:18:29.108
died tragically in a
helicopter crash in 2020.

00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:31.902
Bryant had been arguably the
biggest advocate in the world

00:18:31.902 --> 00:18:32.945
for the women's game.

00:18:32.945 --> 00:18:33.862
And without him,

00:18:33.862 --> 00:18:36.532
it was unclear who would carry that torch.

00:18:36.532 --> 00:18:39.034
That was kind of a big question
when Kobe died was like,

00:18:39.034 --> 00:18:43.622
who was gonna step up and
continue to help fight for women's

00:18:43.622 --> 00:18:46.708
basketball and help
kind of raise the game.

00:18:46.708 --> 00:18:51.713
And I think Steph is doing
a really good job of trying

00:18:52.005 --> 00:18:55.384
inviting women to his camp
and little things like that,

00:18:55.384 --> 00:18:58.137
that are helping to elevate women's game.

00:18:58.137 --> 00:19:02.933
And this deal is incredible
being not just the first NIL

00:19:02.933 --> 00:19:04.226
deal on college athlete,

00:19:04.226 --> 00:19:06.228
but also the first female
assigned to his brand.

00:19:06.228 --> 00:19:08.355
I don't even really know what word to use.

00:19:08.355 --> 00:19:11.441
Describe that feeling when I
first signed it and being here

00:19:11.441 --> 00:19:12.276
now,

00:19:12.276 --> 00:19:13.527
it means so much.

00:19:14.486 --> 00:19:15.320
Azzi's connection to

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.656
and reliance on her own family was on

00:19:17.656 --> 00:19:19.074
full display in LA,

00:19:19.074 --> 00:19:20.617
she'd come to the west coast with her

00:19:20.617 --> 00:19:21.451
mom, dad,

00:19:21.451 --> 00:19:23.954
and two younger brothers and
her success as a burgeoning

00:19:23.954 --> 00:19:24.788
business,

00:19:24.788 --> 00:19:26.957
provide some fun perks.

00:19:26.957 --> 00:19:27.791
On trips like this.

00:19:27.791 --> 00:19:31.503
I love just watching my parents'
reaction because they've

00:19:31.503 --> 00:19:32.337
been in the game.

00:19:32.337 --> 00:19:34.798
They've always played in
college and they played

00:19:34.798 --> 00:19:35.632
professionally.

00:19:35.632 --> 00:19:38.177
So seeing their reaction
to kind of where I am,

00:19:38.177 --> 00:19:39.011
it's just really funny.

00:19:39.011 --> 00:19:39.845
I mean,

00:19:39.845 --> 00:19:42.014
my dad loves being around
all these NBA players.

00:19:42.014 --> 00:19:45.100
My mom loves seeing all
these high level workouts.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:47.227
And so I was seeing them happy.

00:19:47.227 --> 00:19:48.562
It's really fun.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:51.899
Hi.

00:19:51.899 --> 00:19:53.817
Azzi's parents both played division one

00:19:53.817 --> 00:19:55.152
basketball in college

00:19:55.152 --> 00:19:57.029
and coached her throughout her youth,

00:19:57.029 --> 00:19:59.281
which she credits made her the way she is.

00:19:59.281 --> 00:20:01.491
Even if sometimes it's
not so easy to grow up

00:20:01.491 --> 00:20:03.577
with two coaches for parents.

00:20:03.577 --> 00:20:06.830
Part of the reason that I am the way I am

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.956
is because,

00:20:07.956 --> 00:20:09.750
well they didn't really compliment much.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:10.709
So I always had something to work on.

00:20:10.709 --> 00:20:12.711
I was always working hard.

00:20:12.711 --> 00:20:14.171
I think they did a very good job.

00:20:14.171 --> 00:20:16.423
Obviously when I played really bad,

00:20:16.423 --> 00:20:18.091
I would hear about that,

00:20:18.091 --> 00:20:20.928
but they did a really good
job of separating mom and dad

00:20:20.928 --> 00:20:22.095
from coach.

00:20:22.095 --> 00:20:24.056
I remember when I was younger,

00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:25.891
my dad would take me off to
get ice cream and stuff after

00:20:25.891 --> 00:20:26.892
games.

00:20:26.892 --> 00:20:28.769
That was something when
we started coaching

00:20:28.769 --> 00:20:31.897
and we were very cognizant
of not having that coach role

00:20:31.897 --> 00:20:33.148
carry over.

00:20:33.148 --> 00:20:34.942
I harbor things a little more.

00:20:34.942 --> 00:20:37.027
So sometimes they'd go get
ice cream and I'd be like,

00:20:37.027 --> 00:20:37.861
yo,

00:20:37.861 --> 00:20:38.695
she sucked.

00:20:38.695 --> 00:20:39.655
Why are you getting ice cream?

00:20:39.655 --> 00:20:40.489
Doesn't need ice cream.

00:20:40.489 --> 00:20:43.867
But then he got us ice cream too, so.

00:20:43.867 --> 00:20:45.452
When I started to coach her,

00:20:45.452 --> 00:20:47.746
I definitely did not want
to have that contentious

00:20:47.746 --> 00:20:48.789
relationship at all.

00:20:48.789 --> 00:20:52.334
And so the ice cream thing
became a reminder to me,

00:20:52.334 --> 00:20:55.921
a treat to now I get
to go back and be dad.

00:20:58.131 --> 00:21:00.300
Katie Fudd played at NC state

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:02.469
and then Georgetown in the late 1990s,

00:21:02.469 --> 00:21:04.763
as women's basketball was
starting to gain a bit of

00:21:04.763 --> 00:21:05.597
traction.

00:21:05.597 --> 00:21:07.516
And the WNBA was in its formative years.

00:21:07.516 --> 00:21:10.352
She had to deal with inequalities
that she never wanted her

00:21:10.352 --> 00:21:11.228
daughter to face.

00:21:11.228 --> 00:21:13.313
When it came time for
Azzi to pick a school,

00:21:13.313 --> 00:21:15.816
her mom had a big influence.

00:21:15.816 --> 00:21:17.150
When Azzi was getting recruited,

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:19.861
I felt very strongly
about what is the culture.

00:21:19.861 --> 00:21:21.154
And when I was a Georgetown,

00:21:21.154 --> 00:21:22.030
it was kind of,

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:24.074
it's a men's basketball program
and not really much else

00:21:24.074 --> 00:21:25.867
it's evolved since then,

00:21:25.867 --> 00:21:29.246
but our practice time was limited
on the court based on when

00:21:29.246 --> 00:21:30.080
the men practiced,

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.874
or it was just all based around
the men that there's a lot

00:21:32.874 --> 00:21:33.834
of schools that she was looking at,

00:21:33.834 --> 00:21:36.753
where they had some
storied men's programs,

00:21:36.753 --> 00:21:38.880
but how do the players interact?

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.550
How does what's the
culture on the campus like?

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.844
Let's make sure that we're doing
the right thing by both the

00:21:43.844 --> 00:21:45.804
men's and the women's program.

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:48.724
Azzi's parents were able to
go from being her coaches

00:21:48.724 --> 00:21:50.434
to fans in the stands,

00:21:50.434 --> 00:21:53.979
but now have evolved into her
advisory board on her branding

00:21:53.979 --> 00:21:54.813
deals.

00:21:54.813 --> 00:21:58.191
I think we spent the
better part of the pandemic

00:21:58.191 --> 00:21:59.401
on seminars

00:21:59.401 --> 00:22:02.487
and YouTube and listening.

00:22:02.487 --> 00:22:05.324
I probably have a four year
degree in and of itself on NIL,

00:22:05.324 --> 00:22:08.076
just because we're just
making sure we understood it

00:22:08.076 --> 00:22:09.953
as well as we could to help her,

00:22:09.953 --> 00:22:12.456
but also connecting with the right people.

00:22:12.456 --> 00:22:14.291
And we've been very, very fortunate.

00:22:14.291 --> 00:22:15.584
I think the fact that we have

00:22:15.584 --> 00:22:16.835
such a great relationship with her,

00:22:16.835 --> 00:22:18.170
she trusts us implicitly.

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:20.797
We're not gonna put her
in a situation that one,

00:22:20.797 --> 00:22:23.050
she doesn't support the
company or she wants authentic

00:22:23.050 --> 00:22:24.134
stuff.

00:22:24.134 --> 00:22:26.386
And then we're not gonna put
her in a situation that just

00:22:26.386 --> 00:22:27.512
isn't good for her.

00:22:27.512 --> 00:22:28.472
Yeah. I like these.

00:22:28.472 --> 00:22:30.182
I would definitely say
that this past year,

00:22:30.182 --> 00:22:31.350
my freshman year,

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:33.268
it was a little difficult managing.

00:22:33.268 --> 00:22:34.102
I mean,

00:22:34.102 --> 00:22:36.188
I was really lucky to have
my parents so involved,

00:22:36.188 --> 00:22:39.816
so they did a lot of the
background stuff with my agents so

00:22:39.816 --> 00:22:42.652
that I wouldn't need to be on
calls and stuff I could focus

00:22:42.652 --> 00:22:44.905
on school and basketball.

00:22:44.905 --> 00:22:47.616
But I was still trying
to figure my way out,

00:22:47.616 --> 00:22:51.495
navigate my first year of
college while also navigating NIL

00:22:51.495 --> 00:22:52.329
stuff.

00:22:52.329 --> 00:22:54.498
So it did feel a little
overwhelming at times,

00:22:54.498 --> 00:22:56.291
but I think we did a
really good job managing.

00:22:56.291 --> 00:22:57.125
Now,

00:22:57.125 --> 00:22:58.293
looking back on that whole year,

00:22:58.293 --> 00:22:59.669
I feel a lot more comfortable.

00:23:03.006 --> 00:23:05.717
As the new season starts Azzi's
NIL deals existing and new

00:23:05.717 --> 00:23:08.011
will be in the background.

00:23:08.011 --> 00:23:10.555
Expectations are always
high at UConn and even more

00:23:10.555 --> 00:23:13.725
attention will be on her,
given Buecker's injury.

00:23:13.725 --> 00:23:17.229
While new NIL opportunities
grab headlines and attention,

00:23:17.229 --> 00:23:20.649
Azzi has a clear focus on what's ahead.

00:23:20.649 --> 00:23:22.943
How do you raise your NIL game?

00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:26.488
How do you grow it in a way
that's authentically Azzi?

00:23:26.488 --> 00:23:27.322
Well,

00:23:27.322 --> 00:23:30.033
I think now that I have my first
year kind of under my belt,

00:23:30.033 --> 00:23:33.245
I've established my brands
with all these other people,

00:23:33.245 --> 00:23:35.914
but I think I need to be able to

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:39.918
establish my own brand more,

00:23:39.918 --> 00:23:43.880
like the Azzi brand and post
about myself more as well.

00:23:43.880 --> 00:23:47.092
But I think just knowing that
what your priorities are,

00:23:47.092 --> 00:23:49.761
that my priorities right now
are basketball and school,

00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:51.263
'cause without good grades,

00:23:51.263 --> 00:23:52.222
wouldn't be able to play.

00:23:52.222 --> 00:23:53.056
And without basketball,

00:23:53.056 --> 00:23:54.808
I wouldn't have these
opportunities and these deals.

